# Expected conflict — liability cap vs Amendment No. 1 (gold CONF-001)

An ordinary claim on 2026-09-15 is inside both definitions: $720,000 under the Order Form
and $500,000 under the Amendment. SYN-004 § 3.2 removed the tie-breaker, so the answer is
the conflict, not a number. This is the document that ingestion must refuse to merge.

> Using Legal_types as T
> Using Conflict_liability_cap_with_amendment as A

```catala
declaration scope TestAmendmentConflict:
  output computation content A.AmendedLiabilityCap

scope TestAmendmentConflict:
  definition computation equals
    output of A.AmendedLiabilityCap with {
      -- annual_fees: $240,000
      -- claim_type: T.ClaimType.Ordinary
      -- claim_date: |2026-09-15|
    }
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope TestAmendmentConflict
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  During evaluation: conflict between multiple valid consequences for
│  assigning the same variable.
│
├─➤ src/conflict_liability_cap_with_amendment.catala_en:40.24-41:
│    │
│ 40 │     consequence equals annual_fees * 3.0
│    │                        ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
├─ CONFLICT — liability cap with Amendment No. 1 (ACME-NW-MSA-2026)
│  └─ SYN-003 § 5.1 — the Order Form's general cap
│
├─➤ src/conflict_liability_cap_with_amendment.catala_en:54.24-32:
│    │
│ 54 │     consequence equals $500,000
│    │                        ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
└─ CONFLICT — liability cap with Amendment No. 1 (ACME-NW-MSA-2026)
   └─ SYN-004 § 2.1 — the Amendment's flat cap
#return code 123#
```
